ithub.com/users/mxr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mxr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mxr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mxr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mxr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mxr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2026-09-26T23:34:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T14:29:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rhysd/actionlint/pulls/743","html_url":"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/pull/743","diff_url":"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/pull/743.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint/pull/743.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Add the `ubuntu-26.04` and `ubuntu-26.04-arm` runner labels from #683, and fix the unrelated CI failures that blocked it.\n\n| Problem | Solution |\n|---|---|\n| actionlint does not know the `ubuntu-26.04` and `ubuntu-26.04-arm` runner labels. | Carry over the commit from #683 unchanged. |\n| `govulncheck` flags `golang.org/x/net` v0.52.0 in the Lint job. | Bump `golang.org/x/net` to v0.58.0, the newest release that still supports Go 1.25. |\n| The windows-11-arm image has no `winget`, so installing shellcheck fails. | Always install shellcheck with Chocolatey, which is available on all Windows images. |\n| hadolint's new DL3066 rule rejects the non-numeric `USER guest`. | Use `USER 405:100`, the numeric UID:GID of Alpine's `guest` user. |\n| `TestDetectErrorBadRequest` expects an error, but raw.githubusercontent.com now redirects `//v2/action.yml` to a 404. | Replace it with `TestDetectNotFoundForEmptySlug`, which asserts the actual 404 behavior. |\n\nCloses #682. Superse